-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMontellaro2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Montellaro, Zach (April 29, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/29/voting-rights-act-supreme-court-future-00898949\">\"The Voting Rights Act is now a 'dead letter' after latest Supreme Court decision\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Politico\" title=\"Politico\">Politico</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">May 12,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Politico&amp;rft.atitle=The+Voting+Rights+Act+is+now+a+%27dead+letter%27+after+latest+Supreme+Court+decision&amp;rft.date=2026-04-29&amp;rft.aulast=Montellaro&amp;rft.aufirst=Zach&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.politico.com%2Fnews%2F2026%2F04%2F29%2Fvoting-rights-act-supreme-court-future-00898949&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-74\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-74\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFDonegen2026\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Donegen, Moira (April 30, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/apr/30/supreme-court-voting-rights-act-ruling\">\"The supreme court's voting rights decision is a death knell for American democracy\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Guardian\" title=\"The Guardian\">The Guardian</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">May 12,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=The+supreme+court%E2%80%99s+voting+rights+decision+is+a+death+knell+for+American+democracy&amp;rft.date=2026-04-30&amp;rft.aulast=Donegen&amp;rft.aufirst=Moira&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fcommentisfree%2F2026%2Fapr%2F30%2Fsupreme-court-voting-rights-act-ruling&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-75\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-75\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFAnderson2026\" class=\"citation news cs1\"><a href=\"/wiki/Carol_Anderson\" title=\"Carol Anderson\">Anderson, Carol</a> (May 6, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/apr/06/black-voters-louisiana-v-callais-supreme-court\">\"As a supreme court ruling looms, the US is dismantling Black voting power\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Guardian\" title=\"The Guardian\">The Guardian</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">May 12,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=As+a+supreme+court+ruling+looms%2C+the+US+is+dismantling+Black+voting+power&amp;rft.date=2026-05-06&amp;rft.aulast=Anderson&amp;rft.aufirst=Carol&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fcommentisfree%2F2026%2Fapr%2F06%2Fblack-voters-louisiana-v-callais-supreme-court&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-76\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-76\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFBerman2026\" class=\"citation magazine cs1\">Berman, Ari (April 29, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2026/04/supreme-court-louisiana-vra-callais/\">\"Supreme Court Deals a Death Blow to the Voting Rights Act\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Mother_Jones_(magazine)\" title=\"Mother Jones (magazine)\">Mother Jones</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">May 12,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Mother+Jones&amp;rft.atitle=Supreme+Court+Deals+a+Death+Blow+to+the+Voting+Rights+Act&amp;rft.date=2026-04-29&amp;rft.aulast=Berman&amp;rft.aufirst=Ari&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.motherjones.com%2Fpolitics%2F2026%2F04%2Fsupreme-court-louisiana-vra-callais%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-77\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-77\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFVollers2026\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Vollers, Anna Claire (May 4, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://stateline.org/2026/05/04/supreme-court-voting-rights-ruling-set-to-reshape-local-power-from-statehouses-to-school-boards/\">\"Supreme Court voting rights ruling set to reshape local power from statehouses to school boards\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Stateline_(news)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Stateline (news)\">Stateline (news)</a></i>. <q>The U.S. Supreme Court's new decision gutting a key provision of the federal Voting Rights Act clears the way for state officials to drastically reshape not only Congress but also state legislatures, county commissions, city councils and even local school boards.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Stateline+%28news%29&amp;rft.atitle=Supreme+Court+voting+rights+ruling+set+to+reshape+local+power+from+statehouses+to+school+boards&amp;rft.date=2026-05-04&amp;rft.aulast=Vollers&amp;rft.aufirst=Anna+Claire&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fstateline.org%2F2026%2F05%2F04%2Fsupreme-court-voting-rights-ruling-set-to-reshape-local-power-from-statehouses-to-school-boards%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-78\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-78\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFSample\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Sample, James. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://abcnews.com/Politics/5-things-supreme-courts-landmark-decision-voting-rights/story?id=131396119\">\"5 things to know about the Supreme Court's landmark decision on the Voting Rights Act\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/ABC_News_(United_States)\" title=\"ABC News (United States)\">ABC News (United States)</a></i>. <q>Beyond Congress, the ruling will influence state legislative, local, and school board districts nationwide.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=ABC+News+%28United+States%29&amp;rft.atitle=5+things+to+know+about+the+Supreme+Court%27s+landmark+decision+on+the+Voting+Rights+Act&amp;rft.aulast=Sample&amp;rft.aufirst=James&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fabcnews.com%2FPolitics%2F5-things-supreme-courts-landmark-decision-voting-rights%2Fstory%3Fid%3D131396119&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-79\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-79\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFUrell2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Urell, Aaryn (April 30, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://eji.org/news/supreme-court-undermines-black-political-participation-in-devastating-ruling-on-voting-rights-act/\">\"Supreme Court Undermines Black Political Participation in Ruling on Voting Rights Act\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Equal_Justice_Initiative\" title=\"Equal Justice Initiative\">Equal Justice Initiative</a></i>. <q>In a brief to the Supreme Court, the <a href=\"/wiki/Brennan_Center\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Brennan Center\">Brennan Center</a> summarized the impact of Section 2:<br /><br />Indeed, since the 1980s, Section 2 of the Voting Rights Act has played an indispensable role in improving representation on city councils, school boards, county commissions, and other local government bodies across the country.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Equal+Justice+Initiative&amp;rft.atitle=Supreme+Court+Undermines+Black+Political+Participation+in+Ruling+on+Voting+Rights+Act&amp;rft.date=2026-04-30&amp;rft.aulast=Urell&amp;rft.aufirst=Aaryn&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Feji.org%2Fnews%2Fsupreme-court-undermines-black-political-participation-in-devastating-ruling-on-voting-rights-act%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-80\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-80\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFFIELDSCHANDLER2026\" class=\"citation news cs1\">FIELDS, GARY; CHANDLER, KIM (April 30, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-voting-rights-act-louisiana-alabama-4e3225083caccda5ec73a98533a79add\">\"Supreme Court hollows out a landmark law that had protected minority voting rights for 6 decades\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/AP_News\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AP News\">AP News</a></i>. <q>Voting rights experts said the ruling leaves the Voting Rights Act only a shell of what it had been and will provide an open door for political mapmakers at every level — from local school districts to state legislatures to Congress — to undermine minority representation.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=AP+News&amp;rft.atitle=Supreme+Court+hollows+out+a+landmark+law+that+had+protected+minority+voting+rights+for+6+decades&amp;rft.date=2026-04-30&amp;rft.aulast=FIELDS&amp;rft.aufirst=GARY&amp;rft.au=CHANDLER%2C+KIM&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fsupreme-court-voting-rights-act-louisiana-alabama-4e3225083caccda5ec73a98533a79add&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-81\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-81\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFLevineCraftWitherspoon2026\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Levine, Sam; Craft, Will; Witherspoon, Andrew (May 8, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/08/supreme-court-voting-rights-act-misleading-data-doj\">\"Samuel Alito's Voting Rights Act ruling cited misleading data from DoJ\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Guardian\" title=\"The Guardian\">The Guardian</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">May 20,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=Samuel+Alito%E2%80%99s+Voting+Rights+Act+ruling+cited+misleading+data+from+DoJ&amp;rft.date=2026-05-08&amp;rft.aulast=Levine&amp;rft.aufirst=Sam&amp;rft.au=Craft%2C+Will&amp;rft.au=Witherspoon%2C+Andrew&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2026%2Fmay%2F08%2Fsupreme-court-voting-rights-act-misleading-data-doj&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Louisiana&#95;v.&#95;Callais&#95;:13-82\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Louisiana_v._Callais_:13_82-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMorrisMiller2026\" class=\"citation journal cs1\">Morris, Kevin T; Miller, Michael G. (2026). <span class=\"id-lock-subscription\" title=\"Paid subscription required\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1086/739960\">\"Did Shelby County v. Holder Increase the Racial Turnout Gap?\"</a></span>. <i>The Journal of Politics</i>. <a href=\"/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1086%2F739960\">10.1086/739960</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ISSN (identifier)\">ISSN</a>&#160;<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0022-3816\">0022-3816</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Journal+of+Politics&amp;rft.atitle=Did+Shelby+County+v.+Holder+Increase+the+Racial+Turnout+Gap%3F&amp;rft.date=2026&amp;rft&#95;id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1086%2F739960&amp;rft.issn=0022-3816&amp;rft.aulast=Morris&amp;rft.aufirst=Kevin+T&amp;rft.au=Miller%2C+Michael+G.&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.1086%2F739960&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-83\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-83\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-press-distracts-republicans-pocketbook-issues-election-day-rcna598995\">\"Trump's focus on the press distracts Republicans from pocketbook issues ahead of Election Day\"</a>. <i>NBC News</i>. September 22, 2026<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">September 23,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=NBC+News&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+focus+on+the+press+distracts+Republicans+from+pocketbook+issues+ahead+of+Election+Day&amp;rft.date=2026-09-22&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nbcnews.com%2Fpolitics%2Fdonald-trump%2Ftrump-press-distracts-republicans-pocketbook-issues-election-day-rcna598995&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-:1-84\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-:1_84-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-:1_84-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-:1_84-2\"><sup><i><b>c</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFChow\" class=\